{
  "skill": "active-directory-certificates",
  "title": "AD CS Certificate Attacks (ESC1-ESC15)",
  "description": "Exploit Active Directory Certificate Services (AD CS): ESC1 through ESC15 misconfigurations, certificate template and CA abuse, enrollment agent paths, Golden Certificates and certificate-based persistence. Use when a domain has an enterprise CA, when BloodHound or Certipy output shows certificate templates or enrollment rights, when you need a certificate that authenticates as another user or machine, or when reviewing PKI hardening. Covers Certipy, Certify, bloodyAD, ForgeCert, Rubeus and PKINIT abuse.",
